{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-108270",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X<x) \\\\  & =1-0.05 \\\\  & =0.95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(5),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=5.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>1.145)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.145.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
